 "notes": [
  "Step 1 parts kept unchanged: 1 Uno, 1 breadboard, 1 speaker, 3 FSRs, 3x10k + 1x100 ohm resistors, 14 jumper wires.",
  "Breadboard orientation follows the image: the upper half (rows j-f) is bank 'b' and the lower half (rows e-a) is bank 't'. Top rails: tn (black line) and tp (red line); bottom rails: bn and bp. Rail hole indices are approximate; any hole on a rail is the same strip.",
  "Speaker: pin 8 -> blue wire -> 9b.i; the 100 ohm resistor spans 9b.h to 12b.h; the speaker's red lead (port 2) goes in 12b.i and its black lead (port 1) goes to the top ground rail.",
  "Each FSR: red wire to the 5V rail, blue wire to a column that holds the 10k pull-down to ground and a yellow wire to an analog pin. Wiring is FSR3 (col 24) -> A0, FSR2 (col 16) -> A1, FSR1 (col 6) -> A2, as traced from the image.",
  "The 5V rail (tp) is linked to the bottom + rail (bp) and the GND rail (tn) to the bottom - rail (bn) by two long vertical wires at the right edge.",
  "The schematic labels the speaker resistor 10k, but the parts list and text say 100 ohm, so 100 ohm is used.",
  "Arduino GND.1 is used for the ground wire; the image shows the second power-header GND, which is the same net."
 ],
